<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo says China's Jinlong smelter started up.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo says China's Jinlong smelter started up.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Metal Mining Co said on Tuesday that the Jinlong copper smelter in China started operation on April 8. Sumitomo owns 20 percent of the facility.</p>
<p>Sumitomo said in a statement the smelter in Anhui Province would begin production of refined copper in May and would produce 60,000 to 70,000 tonnes by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Japanese trading houses Sumitomo Corp and Itochu Corp also own 7.5 percent each of the Jinlong smelter, which is due to become China's largest copper smelter with annual production capacity of 100,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
